Z||000006||theogre||06-29-2001||08:23 PM||||I'll assume you know what's really going on.... That the WWF corporation really owns WCW. There are not actually two companies anymore.<P>ECW is effectivly the "farm league" for WWF. If you look like an idiot there, you sure as hell aren't making the WWF. ECW's management has direct ties to WWF.<P>WCW has been effectivly dead for a long time. The Turner/Bishoff managment ran that mess into the ground ages ago.<P>I think eventually the WCW will be totally gone. If it ends on a pay per view at least it goes out with a bang. In the mean time we'll get to see some pretty funny stuff with Shane and the "invasion" story lines.<P>WWF's main advantage is that now they have little or no competition in the ratings. ECW is available only at weird hours and only in limited cable markets. WWF is now the only nationally carried program of the type.<P>The secondary advantage is that WWF gains WCW's active contracts. This lets them pick over what few people in WCW might be of interest and dump the rest without allot of negotiations with every individual WCW performer.<P>||||reg||1
